ave connected with a pair or a better high card (Ace-high). Since the pot is small and my hand has some showdown value (beating Q-high, T-high, etc.), but not enough to confidently value bet, and bluffing is risky against a calling station range, the best move is to minimize variance. Checking back realizes my equity without risking more chips.\n\nReason: I have High Card King with a Jack kicker. The opponent has checked to me on the River. The pot is small, and there is no strong reason to bluff given the board texture connects with many random hands (flush draw, straight draw, pairs). Checking is the safest play to see a showdown for free, preserving my chip lead.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
